The ECL 2.0 text is in LICENSE-ECL-2.0. Those terms apply to the translated
files under `src/devices/bsim4/`; the generated interface tables there
(`parameters.rs`, `defaults_data.rs`, `fields.rs`) record names, identifiers
and literal defaults only. The translation modifies the originals: C's
pointers, `CKTcircuit` access and matrix pointers are replaced by the port's
own interfaces (`src/devices/bsim4/host.rs`).

The captured comparison data in `conformance/golden/` is rawfile output produced
by running the upstream `ngspice` binary on the decks in `conformance/netlists/`.
It is committed so that the test suite can run without a C toolchain, and it is
regenerated — never edited — by `cargo xtask golden capture`.
